---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const months=[
 {name:'CTR',value:'6.59–17.78%',note:'campaign range'},
 {name:'Lead conversion',value:'4.17–7.42%',note:'campaign range'},
 {name:'Cost / conversion',value:'€3.25',note:'2024 average'},
 {name:'CPC',value:'€0.20',note:'2024 average'}
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Consilium Medicum — Google Ads case | RM CREATIVES" description="How RM CREATIVES generated 3,356 Google Ads conversions for a medical clinic while working inside healthcare advertising restrictions.">
<main>
<section class="hero shell"><div class="crumb eyebrow"><a href="/cases">CASES</a><span> / CONSILIUM MEDICUM / GOOGLE ADS</span></div><div class="hero-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">MEDICAL CLINIC / GOOGLE SEARCH</span><h1>Demand was not<br/>the problem.<br/><em>Capturing it was.</em></h1></div><div class="intro"><p>People were already searching for doctors and medical services. The job was to turn that intent into measurable enquiries — while navigating the restrictions that make healthcare advertising harder than ordinary search campaigns.</p><span class="eyebrow">CASE DATA / 2024</span></div></div><div class="metrics"><div><strong>3,356</strong><span>Google Ads conversions</span></div><div><strong>€3.25</strong><span>cost per conversion</span></div><div><strong>€0.20</strong><span>average CPC</span></div><div><strong>4.17–7.42%</strong><span>lead conversion range</span></div></div></section>

<section class="case-section shell"><div class="two"><span class="eyebrow">THE PROBLEM</span><div><h2>Healthcare search<br/>is not normal search.</h2><p class="statement">The patient has intent. Google has rules. The clinic needs enquiries.</p><p>Medical campaigns can face restrictions, rejected ads and landing-page compliance issues. Simply building a keyword list and increasing bids does not solve that.</p><p>The acquisition system had to capture existing demand while staying operational when individual ads, claims or landing pages were challenged by platform policy.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="search-stage"><div class="shell"><div class="stage-head"><span class="eyebrow">PATIENT VIEW / HIGH-INTENT SEARCH</span><h2>The journey starts<br/>with a problem.</h2><p>A representative patient journey. The interface is simplified; the performance figures are from the 2024 case data.</p></div><div class="journey">
<div class="step"><span class="num">01</span><div><span class="eyebrow">SEARCH</span><h3>A patient searches for care.</h3><p>Not an audience. Not an impression. A person actively looking for a doctor, test or medical service.</p></div><div class="google"><div class="gbar">G&nbsp;&nbsp; medical clinic Riga <b>⌕</b></div><div class="result"><small>Sponsored · consilium-medicum.lv</small><strong>Medical specialists in Riga</strong><p>Find the right specialist and contact the clinic.</p></div><div class="result organic"><small>consilium-medicum.lv</small><strong>Consilium Medicum</strong></div></div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="num">02</span><div><span class="eyebrow">LANDING PAGE</span><h3>Intent meets the right service.</h3><p>The click has to land on a page that matches the search, explains the service clearly and gives the patient an obvious next action.</p></div><div class="landing"><div class="browserbar"><span>● ● ●</span><b>consilium-medicum.lv</b></div><div class="landbody"><small>CONSILIUM MEDICUM</small><h4>Specialist consultation</h4><p>Information → trust → contact</p><button>CONTACT CLINIC</button></div></div></div>
<div class="step"><span class="num">03</span><div><span class="eyebrow">CONVERSION</span><h3>The click becomes<br/>an enquiry.</h3><p>Calls and lead actions were tracked as conversions, so campaign decisions could be made around patient response rather than traffic alone.</p></div><div class="conversion"><span>GOOGLE ADS / 2024</span><strong>3,356</strong><p>tracked conversions</p><div class="line"><i></i></div><small>Calls + lead actions</small></div></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="case-section dark"><div class="shell"><div class="two"><span class="eyebrow">THE OPERATING MODEL</span><div><h2>Performance inside<br/>the restrictions.</h2><p class="statement">When healthcare advertising rules change what can run, the campaign structure has to adapt without losing the business objective.</p><div class="rules"><div><span>01</span><b>Broader targeting</b><p>Build enough coverage to capture relevant patient demand rather than depending on one fragile campaign.</p></div><div><span>02</span><b>Landing-page compliance</b><p>Align the destination with advertising requirements and the patient’s search intent.</p></div><div><span>03</span><b>Continuous checks</b><p>Watch approvals, restrictions and performance instead of treating campaign launch as the finish line.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section>

<section class="numbers shell"><div class="numbers-head"><span class="eyebrow">PERFORMANCE / 2024</span><h2>Cheap clicks are useless<br/>without patient action.</h2></div><div class="number-grid">{months.map(m=><div class="number-card"><span class="eyebrow">{m.name}</span><strong>{m.value}</strong><small>{m.note}</small></div>)}</div><p class="note">Conversions in the historical case include tracked calls and lead actions. CRM-to-visit attribution was not integrated at the time, so we do not claim a patient or revenue number that was not measured.</p></section>

<section class="case-section accent"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow">THE SYSTEM</span><h2>Capture demand.<br/>Measure response.<br/>Keep improving.</h2><div class="flow"><span>PATIENT NEED</span><b>→</b><span>GOOGLE SEARCH</span><b>→</b><span>RELEVANT AD</span><b>→</b><span>SERVICE PAGE</span><b>→</b><span>CALL / LEAD</span><b>→</b><span>CLINIC</span></div></div></section>

<section class="case-section shell"><div class="two"><span class="eyebrow">WHAT THIS CASE PROVES</span><div><h2>Google Ads can be<br/>an acquisition channel,<br/>not a traffic channel.</h2><p class="statement">3,356 tracked conversions at an average €3.25 per conversion.</p><p>The important part is not the dashboard screenshot. It is the operating model behind it: search intent, relevant landing pages, conversion tracking and active management of healthcare advertising restrictions.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="next dark"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow">NEXT CASE</span><h2>DENTA<br/><em>Acquisition + SEO.</em></h2><a href="/cases">BACK TO CASE LIBRARY ↗</a></div></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
